  {
   "id": "nvidia-ceo-resigns",
   "group": "Tech & AI",
   "headline": "Nvidia's CEO steps down immediately; CFO Kress takes over as interim chief",
   "when": "Thu 12 Nov · US session",
   "what": "Nvidia told the SEC that Jensen Huang resigned as president, chief executive and director, effective immediately. CFO Colette Kress is interim CEO while the board searches for a successor, and she keeps her finance role. Harvey Jones became board chair. Press reports link the exit to alleged affairs. Nvidia shares fell more than 10% in premarket trading, and one market wrap had them about 5% lower after a partial recovery. Nvidia says its quarterly results still come on 17 Nov.",
   "why": "Nvidia sits at the centre of the AI chip trade, so leadership risk spreads to chip makers, the AI and semiconductor funds you hold, and the large-cap index funds where it is a big weight. Your direct NVDA position is small. The next checkpoints are the 17 Nov results and any news on a permanent CEO.",
