   "id": "fed-hike-bets-yields",
   "group": "United States",
   "headline": "Traders now expect a December Fed hike as the 10-year yield tops 5%",
   "when": "Thu 12 Nov · US session",
   "what": "Markets price a 94% chance of a 25 bp Fed hike at the 9 Dec meeting, according to CoinDesk. Governor Waller leans to 25 bp and would consider 50 bp if October inflation stays firm. Cleveland Fed's Hammack prefers smaller, steadier hikes. The 10-year yield closed up 10 bp at 5.10%. The S&P 500 fell 0.35% and the Nasdaq 0.39%.",
   "why": "Higher yields make future profits worth less, which weighs most on large technology shares that dominate your S&P 500 feeder and US fund. A stronger dollar can also lift your THB-priced US funds when converted. The 4 Dec jobs report and the 9 Dec Fed decision are the next tests.",
