   "headline": "Bitcoin sinks to a three-month low as rates rise and an index drops Strategy",
   "when": "Thu 12 Nov",
   "what": "Bitcoin fell about 3.5% to roughly $71,300, its weakest since August. Ether is near $2,000. US spot bitcoin funds lost about $300 million on Wednesday. MSCI will remove Strategy, the largest corporate bitcoin holder, from its global indexes after the close on 30 Nov, which could force funds that track those indexes to sell. Separately, the US Justice Department won court approval to seize or restrain more than $1.2 billion stolen in the Binance hack.",
